  "equipment_type": "Heat pump",
  "applies_to": "Acond air-to-water and brine heat pumps with the ModbusTCP function activated, interface description version 2.35 dated 01.12.2022.",
  "summary": "Acond heat pumps act as a Modbus TCP slave on port 502 once a service technician has activated the function. Input registers report setpoints, sensor temperatures, a status bit field, the operating and regulation mode, fault codes and compressor speed or capacity. Holding registers let the master set room, hot water, pool and cooling targets, choose the mode, acknowledge faults and feed in its own room, outdoor, solar and pool temperatures.",
  "transport": [
    "TCP"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": null,
    "parity": null,
    "data_bits": null,
    "stop_bits": null,
    "tcp_port": 502
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Registers are printed as 30001- (input registers, read with function 4) and 40001- (holding registers, function 3/6/16). Drop the leading 3 or 4 and subtract one: 30007 is input register 6, 40006 is holding register 5."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "Acond Modbus TCP INTERFACE DESCRIPTION",
    "doc_number": "Version 2.35",
    "revision_date": "2022-12-01",
    "url": "https://community.openenergymonitor.org/uploads/short-url/bJsxkmQiygrj9DNip0f8rSOgVU.pdf",
    "unofficial": true,
    "pages": "p. 1 settings; pp. 1-3 input registers; pp. 4-5 holding registers"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Acond's own site does not serve this description publicly (its older v2.34 link returns an HTML page); the link is an unaltered copy of Acond's PDF posted on the OpenEnergyMonitor forum.",
    "Every value is a single 16-bit register: 'Int' rows are INT16 (several have negative minimums printed) and 'Word' rows are bit fields. x10 rows are tenths of a degree.",
    "30020, 30024 and 40014 carry compressor speed in rpm on most series but heat pump power in W on the PRO series; the units field is left blank for that reason.",
    "Bit 5 of 30007 is printed with the same text as bit 4 (circuit 1 pump); it is reproduced as printed. Bits 11 and 13-15 are reserved.",
    "The fault code books referenced by 30021-30023 are not part of this document.",
    "30019 is printed with a x10 modifier but a min/max of 10/25; the x10 scale is kept as printed."
  ],
